# A named train is checked where it is defined; the error points at the
# element at fault inside it.
== SOURCE
u:t_ := [n_ot +]
u:t_ 1 2
== ERROR
error[type-mismatch]: expected Bool or Int, found a -> a
 --> -e:1:10
  |
1 | u:t_ := [n_ot +]
  |          ^^^^
  = note: `n_ot` has type (Truthy a, Truthy b) => a -> b
  = note: in the train `[n_ot +]`, `n_ot` is applied as `n_ot (+ x)`, where x is the train's argument
  = note: `+` takes two arguments, so `+ x` is a function waiting for the other
  = help: this is a function still waiting for an argument: give it one, or quote it ('f_) to pass the function itself
